  "description": "The user is projected onto the overall harmful narrative of the meme, which frames the visual and textual elements as a racialized gender violence trope. The user implicitly identifies with the meme's binary framework, projecting their own understanding or biases onto the juxtaposed victims and the racialized labels. The user is not explicitly directed to a specific visual or textual element with deictic pronouns, but the entire scene functions as a projection of the user's internalized stereotypes onto the visual material and textual labels.",
